# THE THIRD ODDS CREDENTIAL. Five of its six copies were in THIS repo.
#
# Three odds keys exist. The free-tier key above was removed 2026-08-25 and
# pinned at 0. The live 20K-plan key was rotated by the owner 2026-09-15 and was
# never a literal anywhere. This is the Starter-tier key held by
# env.ODDS_API_KEY_FALLBACK in field-relay-nba. It was never rotated.
#
# Measured 2026-10-12 by hashing every 32-hex token in all four repos:
#   .coderabbit.yaml                            1
#   docs/CC-CMD-2026-06-16-odds-quota-audit.md  1
#   outbox/cc-odds-audit-results.md             3
#   (field-relay-nba held the sixth; field-laboratory and field-playground 0)
#
# WHY NO GATE SAW IT: a ratchet only knows the hashes it is given. This
# scanner reported PASS on every run while five copies of an undeclared odds
# key sat in tracked files. The 2026-08-25 redaction pass replaced the
# free-tier key with "<redacted 2026-08-25 ...>" on lines ADJACENT to these in
# outbox/cc-odds-audit-results.md and left these standing, because that pass
# chased one known value rather than scanning for credential-shaped tokens.
#
# .coderabbit.yaml:26 was a review instruction reading "never hardcode the
# Starter key (<the key>)" — an instruction against hardcoding a credential,
# with the credential in it.
#
# ZERO, and the literals are gone as of 2026-10-12. The VALUE IS DEAD TOO: the
# owner rotated it at the provider the same day. This repo's git history still
# holds the old literals — history was not rewritten — but they no longer read
# out a credential.
#
# The ratchet stays at zero regardless. A dead key in a document is how the
# free-tier entry above began, and that one is still being chased through four
# repos' history. Zero is about the habit.
#
# See field-relay-nba/docs/CC-CMD-2026-10-12-starter-key-exposure.md.

