# NOT zero, and deliberately so. Nine occurrences, of which THREE are live code:
#
#   workers/field-claude-proxy/src/index.js:105
#       `env.RELAY_SHARED_SECRET || '<literal>'` — an auth comparison. The env
#       read already exists; the literal is its fallback.
#   scripts/seed-mls-return-2026.py:17
#   scripts/seed-mls-tournaments-2026.py:21
#       bare literals in an X-FIELD-Relay header aimed at POST /d1/execute
#   retry_telemetry_probe.js:37
#       same, a fourth live site
#
# The remaining five are prose: CONTRACTS.md:245, three CC-CMDs, one root-cause
# doc.
#
# Removing them WITHOUT rotating first buys nothing — the value is in git
# history either way. The order is written down in field-relay-nba
# docs/CC-CMD-2026-08-25-rotate-relay-secret.md, and it is SOURCE-FIRST: while
# the value is unchanged, replacing a literal with a binding holding the same
# value is a runtime no-op that can be verified live, whereas rotate-first makes
# every site wrong at once.
#
# That CC-CMD counted 114 sites in the relay alone. These nine are additional
# and are named there now.
